ndividually.\n\n- The function $f(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}$ is continuous and differentiable on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ In particular, it  is continuous on $[0,e]$ and differentiable on $(0,e).$ Therefore, $f(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function  $g(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is not defined at $x=0,$ so it is not continuous at $x=0,$ which means it is not continuous on $[0,e].$ Therefore, $g(x)$ does not satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $h(x)={e}^{-x/2}$ is continuous and differentiable on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ In particular, it  is continuous on $[0,e]$ and differentiable on $(0,e).$ Therefore, $h(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\nTherefore, only functions I and III satisfy the conditions for the mean value theorem over the interval $[0,e].$" 13194139534844 true] [17592186314152 1000 #edb/ref 17592186314153 13194139534844 true] [17592186314152 1000 #edb/ref 17592186314154 13194139534844 true] [17592186314152 1000 #edb/ref 17592186314155 13194139534844 true] [17592186314152 1000 #edb/ref 17592186314156 13194139534844 true] [17592186314152 1000 #edb/ref 17592186314157 13194139534844 true] [17592186314152 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534844 true] [17592186314152 1041 "selection" 13194139534844 true] [17592186314152 1104 #edb/ref 17592186314155 13194139534844 true] [17592186314152 1110 #uuid "83ca8298-6a28-5a18-8212-0ae536c8648f" 13194139534844 true] [17592186314153 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139534844 true] [17592186314153 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534844 true] [17592186314153 1111 #uuid "d810bbd6-15e1-5441-a5b8-99651b3eea8b" 13194139534844 true] [17592186314154 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534844 true] [17592186314154 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534844 true] [17592186314154 1111 #uuid "6b6ccab4-a34e-52dd-85e1-d7214cc3bfa5" 13194139534844 true] [17592186314155 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534844 true] [17592186314155 1103 #edb/ref 175921860454