 function $s(x)$ has vertical asymptotes at $x=\\pm 1.$ Hence, $s(x)$ is not continuous on $[-1,1].$ Therefore, $s(x)$ does not satisfiy the conditions of the mean value theorem." 13194139534844 true] [17592186314159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186314160 13194139534844 true] [17592186314159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186314161 13194139534844 true] [17592186314159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186314162 13194139534844 true] [17592186314159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186314163 13194139534844 true] [17592186314159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186314164 13194139534844 true] [17592186314159 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534844 true] [17592186314159 1041 "selection" 13194139534844 true] [17592186314159 1104 #edb/ref 17592186314160 13194139534844 true] [17592186314159 1110 #uuid "43e165b1-ef88-519e-80a6-6a1ee85a6ea2" 13194139534844 true] [17592186314160 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/assets/b246b2835d856e4ec43bd9a96275ddf5531b7d653d46e5c58ae9553b6b59956e.png" 13194139534844 true] [17592186314160 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534844 true] [17592186314160 1111 #uuid "eb037793-c00e-51a0-b7e9-19ff2a8b5b7a" 13194139534844 true] [17592186314161 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/assets/45db5f9f600f29e91fb40335f80fb28bb12f87fc4618c623354b91408f6bb09c.png" 13194139534844 true] [17592186314161 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534844 true] [17592186314161 1111 #uuid "28f4edb0-b2e0-5f2d-b31b-e20351847375" 13194139534844 true] [17592186314162 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/assets/c4c45b3d88dd9821c1c5650e898d806b8887838c609548296040feae8915e40b.png" 13194139534844 true] [17592186314162 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534844 true] [17592186314162 1111 #uuid "aee0cde4-4274-5c11-a1a6-35951fd3a6b3" 13194139534844 true] [17592186314163 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/assets/09017ce160eb