ontinuous on $[0,2].$ Therefore, $t(x)$ does not satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $g(x)$  is continuous on $[0,2]$ but has a cusp at $x=1.$  Hence, it is not differentiable at $x=1,$ which means it is not differentiable on $(0,2).$  Therefore, $g(x)$ does not satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function  $h(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=1.$ Hence, it  is not continuous on $[0,2].$ Therefore, $h(x)$ does not satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function  $s(x)$ is continuous on $[0,2]$ but has a corner point at $x=1.$   Hence, it is not differentiable at $x=1,$ which means it is not differentiable on $(0,2).$  Therefore, $s(x)$ does not satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem." 13194139534844 true] [17592186314204 1000 #edb/ref 17592186314205 13194139534844 true] [17592186314204 1000 #edb/ref 17592186314206 13194139534844 true] [17592186314204 1000 #edb/ref 17592186314207 13194139534844 true] [17592186314204 1000 #edb/ref 17592186314208 13194139534844 true] [17592186314204 1000 #edb/ref 17592186314209 13194139534844 true] [17592186314204 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534844 true] [17592186314204 1041 "selection" 13194139534844 true] [17592186314204 1104 #edb/ref 17592186314205 13194139534844 true] [17592186314204 1110 #uuid "fd0f4dbf-cf67-5f73-875e-61529e6a23cc" 13194139534844 true] [17592186314205 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/assets/e6ccc7f465d50c13059b93e1b12b80bc3c10b9970ea0fedd5a3b3b9d4d3cabf5.png" 13194139534844 true] [17592186314205 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534844 true] [17592186314205 1111 #uuid "3e0e4c7c-830f-5964-85e7-b5bb9f9c8b90" 13194139534844 true] [17592186314206 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/assets/78a7985112e69fa2a647ad4548791ef42bee13c458d1e160199f767771315513.png" 13194139534844 true] [17592186314206 1103 #edb/ref 